  - secure research
  - microdata
  - k-anonymity
  - referential integrity
abstract: >-
  oissyntheticdata is a zero-dependency, pure-Python tool that generates
  structurally faithful synthetic data for secure research environments without
  the synthesizer ever reading the confidential microdata. An on-premises stage
  emits a disclosure-controlled profile of the real data (robust numeric bounds,
  k-suppressed categorical levels, format signatures for identifiers, and the
  distribution of group sizes for fan-out keys); an off-premises stage rebuilds
  a synthetic dataset from that profile alone, preserving column types, ranges,
  category levels, missingness, ID formats and cross-file referential integrity;
  and an inside-only control stage scores structural fidelity. The synthetic
  data is built for code-path coverage so analysts can develop and debug
  off-site, then run the final analysis on the real data on-premises. Maintained
  by OIS.
